  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/stamp_sweep.rs`. It gives the exact distance from a tool axis that moves along a straight line (a parallelogram) to each facet. It uses the triangle-triangle distance law: vertex-to-triangle and edge-to-edge candidates, and an edge-crossing test.\n- `stamp_rise::rapid_rise` uses this exact sweep. The old proof sampled the ball and the flank every r/2. The swept tool must now stay at least as far from the part as the start pose.\n- The plan's own RAPID rises under a held lean now go through the same proof (`stamp_rise::rise_kind`). If the straight rise is not proved, the rapid moves out along the contact normal first, under the same pose (`normal_exit`). Then it rises, and then it crosses to the plan's top point. The exact sweep proves each leg. If no exit is proved, the rapid stays as the plan wrote it, and the verifier's rapid law judges it.\n- `stamp.rs` posts the two via points of such an exit as rapids under the held pose. `stamp_link::contact_normal` is now `pub(super)`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe nine flagged moves are not the #48 feed rises. They are the plan's own retract rapids at the end of each side-pass level. The stamp gave each plan rapid the held lying pose, and nothing proved it. #4108 added the vertical-rapid sweep to the verifier, and this exposed them. The verifier is correct: each lift goes into the part by 0.013 to 0.24 mm.\n\nA second gap was also real. The sampled proof did not see a facet edge between two samples. Move 2141 starts under the tube's equator. With only the rapid route fixed, the sampled proof still accepts move 2141.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (motion lib, `multiaxis::stamp_rise` / `multiaxis::stamp_sweep`):\n\n- `a_rise_that_brushes_an_edge_between_samples_keeps_its_feed`: red on unchanged code.\n- `a_rise_whose_flank_sweeps_a_vertex_between_samples_keeps_its_feed`: red on unchanged code.\n- `a_plan_rapid_up_from_the_contact_must_prove_its_rise_too`: new route (it fails when the normal exit is removed).\n- `the_gap_is_exact_for_a_vertex_an_edge_and_a_face`, `a_degenerate_sweep_reads_its_segment_and_far_facets_are_capped`: the sweep law.\n- The heavy tests of the issue, `swarf_generates_blade_lying_axes_and_verifies_clean_full_band` and `advanced_swarf_adds_the_coarse_rungs_full_band` (app, release, `--ignored`): `0 passed; 2 failed` with nine `RapidInPart` on upstream/main `62456d0a6`, `2 passed` with the fix.\n\nMutations (each one alone, then restored):\n\n- Normal exit removed (`rise_kind` returns the plan rapid as is): the plan-rapid pin is red, and the two heavy tests are red with the same nine warnings.\n- The old sampled law put back in `rapid_rise`: the two between-samples pins are red, and the two heavy tests are red with `RapidInPart { at: 2141 }`.\n\nGates on the final head `ac9cfe056`, base upstream/main `62456d0a6`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 41 steps, 0 failed. This includes `motion suites: swarf_pose_continuity` (the air-link ratchet does not change), `app suites: example_catalog*`, `app suites: operations`, `app suites: posed_contact`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Targeted heavy steps: `motion heavy: multiaxis` ok (256 s), `app heavy: operations` ok (73 s), `app heavy: first_traverse_posed` ok.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changed. The example catalog suites ran green, and they compare the recorded programs.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full heavy lanes (115 steps). Under AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\", they run at the cut.\n- The column radius of the proof is the ball radius, as in `flank_clear`. A shank or holder wider than the ball is not in this proof. The verifier's stack law judges it.\n- The link law's own retract along the normal (`retract_length`) still samples every r/2. This PR does not change it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `stamp.rs`, `stamp_rise.rs`, `stamp_link.rs` or `multiaxis/mod.rs`. The branch merges cleanly with upstream/main `e902ee488`.\n\nChangelog: Swarf: each exit rise under a lying tool is now proved with an exact swept-tool distance, and a retract rapid that cannot rise straight up leaves along the contact normal first. The full-band blade programs verify clean again.\n\nFixes #4315\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
